      "id": "skip-turn-relay-allow",
      "kind": "repository-identity-remap",
      "workflowFile": ".github/workflows/buildtest.yaml",
      "jobId": "test",
      "fromPattern": "go test -race -json -v ./...",
      "toReplacement": "go test -race -json -v -skip '^TestTurnRelay$/^allow$' ./...",
      "expectedMatches": 1,
      "reason": "Owner decision 2026-11-16 ~11:38 AM PST: skip exactly one subtest, TestTurnRelay/allow (package test), identically in every setup. It hard-codes 10.0.0.0/8 and 192.168.0.0/16 as the allowed TURN relay ranges; StarSling runners sit in 172.16.0.0/12 (also RFC 1918; seen 172.20.103.196), so it fails there (diag-1 job 133550338104) and passes on GitHub (10.1.x). The parent TestTurnRelay and its other subtests still run. Test step only; no job, step or if: changed; not a lever target.",
